<resources>

    <!--
      The TV variant of AppTheme.

      `values-television` is Android's UI-mode resource qualifier, and it is
      selected by the same signal as everything else in the app that asks "is
      this a television": UiModeManager.getCurrentModeType() ==
      UI_MODE_TYPE_TELEVISION, which is what MainActivity checks to pin the
      orientation and what React Native reports as Platform.isTV. One signal,
      three readers, so a device cannot be a TV to one of them and a phone to
      another.

      windowFullscreen is the whole difference. A TV genuinely has no status or
      navigation bar, and some TV-mode devices (a tablet in a dock, an emulator
      built from a phone image) do have them and should not: a 10-foot UI leaves
      no room for phone furniture, and safe-area insets are reported as zero on
      TV, so nothing would pad for it anyway.
    -->
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="AppThemeBase">
        <item name="android:windowFullscreen">true</item>
    </style>

</resources>
